  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml`, job `freebsd`: the VM gets `mem: 12288` (was 5120). The build runs `cargo build -j 2`. Nothing else changed in that job.\n- `.github/workflows/freebsd-backfill.yml` (new): starts by hand only, with `workflow_dispatch` and the input `tag`. It has three jobs:\n  - `validate` (read only): checks that the tag has the form `vX.Y.0`, that the tag exists, that its release exists, and that the release has no FreeBSD archive.\n  - `build` (read only): checks out `refs/tags/<tag>`, then runs the VM steps and the archive checks of the `freebsd` job.\n  - `attach` (`contents: write`): refuses a release that already has a FreeBSD archive, runs `gh release upload` without `--clobber`, and removes the line \"FreeBSD (tar.gz) build did not succeed\" from the release body. It runs no code from the tag.\n- `.claude/skills/runners/SKILL.md`: one bullet that lists the new workflow.\n- `docs/decisions/2378-freebsd-backfill.md`: the decision record.\n\nThe build and the upload are in separate jobs. GitHub sets permissions per job. A write step inside the build job would give the built code a write token.\n\n## Memory value\n\n12288 MB. The hosted `ubuntu-24.04` runner has 16 GB. The vmactions/freebsd-vm README gives the default (6144 MB) and no maximum. The value is not measured.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nNone. This change is YAML only. The workflow files parse with PyYAML. The body filter was checked on a sample body.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nEverything. No workflow run started. No `release.yml` run and no backfill run were made. Not checked: the VM build with `-j 2` and 12 GB, the `validate` checks, the upload, and the body edit.\n\nAfter the merge, the maintainer starts the backfill by hand:\n\n    gh workflow run freebsd-backfill.yml -f tag=v0.23.0\n\n## Process change\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nThe runners skill is a process file (`.claude/skills/`). `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` is not edited.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: low\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #2378\n",
